  "prompt": "Design a simple one-storey house within a 10 m × 14 m site, with a total enclosed footprint no greater than 85 m². Include one living room at least 16 m², two bedrooms each at least 9 m², and one bathroom at least 4 m². The main entry faces south; each bedroom is connected to the living room through an accessible circulation path and every specified doorway must be an actual wall cutout at least 0.80 m clear width. Use one floor slab, 0.15 m nominal wall thickness, 2.8 m nominal wall height, and one simple roof. The coordinate system is metres, right-handed, +Z up, north at +Y. Give shared walls exactly one owning module. Build from named modules, validate, revise the living-room doorway from 0.90 m to 0.95 m without rewriting unrelated modules, then compile one deterministic BOMC 1.2 file. Return manifest/revisions, validation failures and recoveries, compiled SHA256, independent Editor and Model-Eval import results, and per-run token/tool/time/memory statistics. If a tool or evidence is unavailable, report NOT_RUN; do not invent success.",
